WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.657
Email cleaning is another good example of safe representation changes.

00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:10.072
The query trims spaces around the email, converts a blank result to null,

00:00:10.072 --> 00:00:13.507
and then converts the remaining text to lowercase.

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:21.542
For example, an email stored with spaces around it and uppercase letters can become a consistent lowercase value without

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:23.892
changing the intended address.

00:00:24.693 --> 00:00:27.125
Why convert blank text to null?

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:35.055
Because it gives us a consistent representation for a missing email and makes later filtering and counting easier.

00:00:35.055 --> 00:00:41.375
But remember, lowercasing and trimming do not prove that the email actually exists.

00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.970
They only standardize the text.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.050
Later, we will perform a structural validation check.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.660
Even that will only tell us whether the text looks like an email address,

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.934
not whether messages can actually be delivered to it.
